# Blocks the gates could not judge, which someone checked another way.
#
# G2 marks a block `not-evaluated` when Trivy has no check for its kind (a
# Rollout, a PyTorchJob, a List), or returned nothing for the file. G3 marks a
# block `missing-crd` when the cluster lacks its custom resource definition.
# Neither is a pass. If such a block holds a pod template, the gate exits 1
# unless the block is listed here, because the pod template went unread.
#
# One entry per line:
#
#     chapter | what | reason
#
# chapter  the path under full-guide/, for example 05-security/02-pod-security.md
# what     what the gate printed for the block: a kind such as Rollout, or
#          no-scanner-result. A block with several is allowed only when all
#          of them are listed. `*` allows every one in that chapter.
# reason   how the block was checked instead, for example "rendered with
#          the chart and run through Trivy in the pull request". Required.
#
# The pull request that adds a line must also say how the block was checked.
# Remove the line when the chapter stops needing it.
15-day-to-day-production-ops/06-progressive-delivery-in-production.md | Rollout | Checked by hand against the 01.01 baseline, and by jsonschema against the rollouts.argoproj.io CRD of argo-rollouts chart 2.43.8 (app v1.10.1), extracted with helm template. sf-pilot has no Argo Rollouts CRD, so the server dry-run cannot run there.
14-eks-in-production-a-to-z/16-developer-experience-for-k8s-teams.md | Config | skaffold.yaml is a Skaffold build config that only the skaffold CLI reads. Its manifests entry lists the 2.2 block, which the static and admission gates check. Its keys follow the Skaffold v4beta14 schema (manifests.rawYaml, deploy.kubectl), checked against the upstream config.go; skaffold itself was not run.
full-guide/examples/bookstore-platform/ml/training-workflow.yaml | WorkflowTemplate | each of the four templates was rendered to a Pod (template securityContext, volumes and container, token setting from the workflow spec) and scanned with Trivy: no core check (KSV-0012, KSV-0014, KSV-0001, KSV-0003, KSV-0030) fails; KSV-0011 (no CPU limit, by baseline 01.03), KSV-0036 (token mounted for the Argo executor, dedicated ServiceAccount) and KSV-0125 are reported and accepted; transcript evidence/13-08.txt, section 4
full-guide/examples/bookstore-platform/observability/otel-collector.yaml | OpenTelemetryCollector | The operator renders this CR into a DaemonSet from its securityContext and podSecurityContext, which set the restricted fields. The CR was checked against the v1beta1 CRD schema of chart 0.115.0 (no unknown fields, no schema errors) and its config passed otelcol-contrib validate in the pinned image (13.09 transcript). The operator-rendered pods were not dry-run, because the CRD is not installed in the lab.
full-guide/examples/bookstore-platform/search/debezium-connector.yaml | KafkaConnect | Strimzi 0.40.0 CR with no Trivy check. Its pod template was checked by hand against the chart's CRD schema (helm pull strimzi-kafka-operator 0.40.0): connectContainer and pod securityContext are set, and each plugin artifact carries a sha512sum.
full-guide/examples/bookstore-platform/search/debezium-connector.yaml | KafkaUser | Strimzi 0.40.0 CR with no Trivy check and no pod template. Its fields were checked against the chart's CRD schema (helm pull strimzi-kafka-operator 0.40.0), with no unknown fields.
full-guide/examples/bookstore-platform/search/debezium-connector.yaml | KafkaConnector | Strimzi 0.40.0 CR with no Trivy check and no pod template. Its fields were checked against the chart's CRD schema (helm pull strimzi-kafka-operator 0.40.0), with no unknown fields.
full-guide/examples/bookstore/argocd/rollouts/catalog-rollout.yaml | Rollout | Read by hand against the 01.01 baseline: automount off with the catalog-sa ServiceAccount, runAsNonRoot with UID and GID 65532, RuntimeDefault seccomp, no privilege escalation, read-only root with an emptyDir for the writable path, drop ALL, requests and a memory limit, a locally built image tag. Its spec.template parses equal to the pod template of raw-manifests/10-catalog-deploy.yaml, and that template wrapped in a Deployment passes Trivy v0.76.1 on all five core checks.
full-guide/examples/bookstore/kustomize/components/kyverno/70-kyverno-policy.yaml | ClusterPolicy | Not a workload. The `containers` key sits inside validate.pattern, which Kyverno matches against Pods, so the file holds no pod template to run. Read by hand: three rules on kind Pod in namespace bookstore, action Audit. It parses to the same policy as raw-manifests/70-kyverno-policy.yaml.
full-guide/examples/bookstore/raw-manifests/70-kyverno-policy.yaml | ClusterPolicy | Not a workload. The `containers` key sits inside validate.pattern, which Kyverno matches against Pods, so the file holds no pod template to run. Read by hand: three rules on kind Pod in namespace bookstore, action Audit. The Kustomize component and the chart's template carry the same three rules.
full-guide/examples/bookstore/helm/bookstore [helm template -f values-prod.yaml] | PrometheusRule | CRD kind the gate cannot judge, in a render that also holds the chart's workloads, so the block reads as holding a pod template. Checked by parsing the render: the 5 documents of the CRD kinds listed for this block contain no containers or template key. The workloads in the same render come from the same templates as the default render, which the gate judges and passes.
full-guide/examples/bookstore/helm/bookstore [helm template -f values-prod.yaml] | ScaledObject | CRD kind the gate cannot judge, in a render that also holds the chart's workloads, so the block reads as holding a pod template. Checked by parsing the render: the 5 documents of the CRD kinds listed for this block contain no containers or template key. The workloads in the same render come from the same templates as the default render, which the gate judges and passes.
full-guide/examples/bookstore/helm/bookstore [helm template -f values-prod.yaml] | ServiceMonitor | CRD kind the gate cannot judge, in a render that also holds the chart's workloads, so the block reads as holding a pod template. Checked by parsing the render: the 5 documents of the CRD kinds listed for this block contain no containers or template key. The workloads in the same render come from the same templates as the default render, which the gate judges and passes.
full-guide/examples/bookstore/helm/bookstore [helm template -f values-prod.yaml] | TriggerAuthentication | CRD kind the gate cannot judge, in a render that also holds the chart's workloads, so the block reads as holding a pod template. Checked by parsing the render: the 5 documents of the CRD kinds listed for this block contain no containers or template key. The workloads in the same render come from the same templates as the default render, which the gate judges and passes.
full-guide/examples/bookstore/helm/bookstore [helm template -f values-staging.yaml] | PrometheusRule | CRD kind the gate cannot judge, in a render that also holds the chart's workloads, so the block reads as holding a pod template. Checked by parsing the render: the 3 documents of the CRD kinds listed for this block contain no containers or template key. The workloads in the same render come from the same templates as the default render, which the gate judges and passes.
full-guide/examples/bookstore/helm/bookstore [helm template -f values-staging.yaml] | ServiceMonitor | CRD kind the gate cannot judge, in a render that also holds the chart's workloads, so the block reads as holding a pod template. Checked by parsing the render: the 3 documents of the CRD kinds listed for this block contain no containers or template key. The workloads in the same render come from the same templates as the default render, which the gate judges and passes.
11-advanced-production-patterns/10-platform-engineering.md | DeploymentRuntimeConfig | Trivy has no check for this kind, so its pod template went unread by the scanner. The template was checked against the upstream v1beta1 CRD schema at Crossplane v2.4.3, and the probe in step 1 checked the chart's pod template. The live pods were not run in this revision.
11-advanced-production-patterns/10-platform-engineering.md | DeploymentRuntimeConfig | Trivy has no check for this kind, so its pod template went unread by the scanner. The template was checked against the upstream v1beta1 CRD schema at Crossplane v2.4.3, and the probe in step 1 checked the chart's pod template. In the lab, the provider pod ran with this runtime config and its securityContext was read back from the live pod (evidence/11-10.txt).
08-day-2-operations/01-cluster-lifecycle.md | no-scanner-result | kind cluster config (kind.x-k8s.io/v1alpha4): it creates nodes, not Pods. The node image is the digest the kind v0.33.0 release notes list for v1.37.0, the digest examples/security-lab/kind/cluster.yaml also pins. kind reads the file itself, so no Pod template reaches Trivy.
08-day-2-operations/01-cluster-lifecycle.md | Cluster | the same kind cluster config: its kind is Cluster from kind.x-k8s.io/v1alpha4, which no cluster serves, so the admission dry run cannot judge it. It creates nodes, not Pods, and its node image is the digest the kind v0.33.0 release notes list for v1.37.0.
05-security/07-admission-control-and-policy-as-code.md | ClusterPolicy | the Kyverno ClusterPolicy in this chapter matches Pods with a pattern over spec.containers, so it is not a Pod. The lab's full mode applies it on a throwaway kind cluster (steps 9 and 10 of labs/05-07.sh); the shared run does not reach it, and the chapter marks it not run
full-guide/examples/bookstore/ml/train/recommender-pytorchjob.yaml | PyTorchJob | No Trivy check exists for PyTorchJob. Checked by reading its pod templates against the restricted fields the other training Pods use. The chapter's server dry run was refused only because no PyTorchJob CRD is installed on the lab (captured in 12/04). Dry-run it again once the Training Operator is installed.
full-guide/examples/bookstore/ml/train/recommender-pytorchjob.yaml | PyTorchJob | No Trivy check exists for PyTorchJob. Its pod templates were checked by reading them against the restricted fields the other training Pods use. The Training Operator also adds an init container to each worker, and those templates do not show it. That container was checked by a server dry run of the worker Pod shape (pytorch-worker-pod-check.yaml, captured in 12/04). The same Pod with the operator's default template is refused, and with the template in operators/training-operator it is admitted. The PyTorchJob CRD is not installed on the lab, so the chapter's server dry run of the PyTorchJob itself is captured only as no matches for the kind. Dry-run it again once the Training Operator is installed.
full-guide/examples/bookstore/ml/train/recommender-rayjob.yaml | RayJob | No Trivy check exists for RayJob. Checked by reading its head, worker and submitter pod templates against the restricted fields. The chapter's server dry run was refused only because no RayJob CRD is installed on the lab (captured in 12/04). The image needs the recommender's packages on top of the Ray base before the file can run. Dry-run it again once KubeRay is installed.
full-guide/examples/bookstore/ml/train/operators/training-operator [kustomize build] | ValidatingWebhookConfiguration | Trivy has no check for ValidatingWebhookConfiguration, so the webhook of the pinned Training Operator v1.9.4 release is not scanned. It carries no pod template. The overlay's Deployment and ClusterRole are scanned, and their findings are accepted with statements in .trivyignore.yaml. The chapter (12.04 step 1) names the upstream file that the webhook comes from.
full-guide/examples/bookstore/ml/batch/recommender-jobset.yaml | JobSet | No Trivy check exists for JobSet. Checked by reading its pod template against the restricted fields the Job files in this chapter use (runAsNonRoot, a non-root UID, dropped capabilities, RuntimeDefault seccomp, no privilege escalation, a read-only root, an emptyDir-only volume). The lab also installed JobSet 0.11.1 and Kueue 0.17.0 and applied this file with only the namespace name replaced: a restricted namespace admitted both worker Pods and the gang ran to Completed (transcript evidence/12-03.txt, install run). The cluster the admission gate uses has no JobSet CRD, so the gate's own dry run cannot read it.
12-kubernetes-for-machine-learning/06-model-serving-and-inference.md | InferenceService | No Trivy check exists for InferenceService, and the KServe CRD is not installed on the lab cluster, so neither the static gate nor the admission dry-run can read its predictor. The block was checked another way: step 8 of lab 12.06 rendered the kserve-crd v0.21.0 chart and found every predictor field the manifest sets in the v1beta1 schema, and its baseline matches recommender-deployment.yaml. Dry-run it again once KServe is installed.
